<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Tunip</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1300 BCE (approx.) · capital Tunip</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tunip, a Syrian city of the Orontes valley caught between Egypt, Mitanni and the Hittites in the Late Bronze Age.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tunip lay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes</a> region of western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>; its site is uncertain. It appears in the 15th century BCE among the cities that resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a>, as an ally of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kadesh">Kadesh</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government, though a council of citizens appears to have shared power. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>, the people of Tunip wrote to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> begging him to restore the son of their former ruler and protect them from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aziru">Aziru</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-amurru">Kingdom of Amurru</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tunip passed under Hittite control in the 14th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> attacked it during his Syrian wars, and it fades from the record in the 13th century BCE.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tunip.jpg" alt="Tunip" width="320" height="356"><figcaption>Image: Nina M. Davies · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foreigners,_Tomb_of_Menkheperraseneb_MET_DP161251.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1300 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tunip</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Syrian Semitic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1400&amp;focus=tunip" aria-label="Tunip on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5635 918 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tunip lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5996 1079h0M5863 1489h0M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5955 1174h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5955 1174h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Syria. <a href="/atlas?year=-1400&amp;focus=tunip">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

